#. command help: didact pack enable
#: didact/commands/packs.py
msgid ""
"One game system is in use at a time: the open world's. A world keeps the system it\n"
"was made with, so enabling a system only gives one to a world that has none yet;\n"
"another system plays in a world of its own (`didact world new <id> --system <pack>`).\n"
"A pack that needs another system (a setting written for it) can't be added either."
msgstr ""
"Bare ett spillsystem er i bruk om gangen: den åpne verdenens. En verden beholder systemet\n"
"den ble opprettet med, så å aktivere et system gir bare et til en verden som ikke har noe ennå;\n"
"et annet system spilles i en egen verden (`didact world new <id> --system <pack>`).\n"
"En pakke som trenger et annet system (en spillverden skrevet for det), kan heller ikke legges til."

#. command help: didact search
#: didact/commands/reference.py
msgid ""
"One ranked list across every source (every word must appear; titles count most).\n"
"Each hit ends with the command that shows it. Records follow player-safe rules\n"
"unless you pass --gm. Sources: rules, terms, mechanics, tables, compendium, records,\n"
"transcript, docs."
msgstr ""
"Én rangert liste på tvers av alle kilder (hvert ord må forekomme; titler teller mest).\n"
"Hvert treff slutter med kommandoen som viser det. Oppslag følger reglene for hva spillerne kan se"
"\n"
"med mindre du oppgir --gm. Kilder: rules, terms, mechanics, tables, compendium, records,\n"
"transcript, docs."

